# Beget CDN settings

## DNS and resource

- Origin `${BEGET_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}`: `A` -> `${ORIGIN_IP}`.
- Create the Beget CDN resource with the origin type **domain name** and value
  `${BEGET_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}`. The resource origin cannot be changed later.
- Technical edge domain: `${BEGET_CDN_SYSTEM_DOMAIN}`.
- Optional custom edge domain: `${BEGET_CDN_CUSTOM_DOMAIN_DISPLAY}`.
- Selected Remnawave Host domain: `${BEGET_HOST_DOMAIN}`.
- Never point `${BEGET_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}` to `*.begetcdn.cloud`.
- A custom domain added in the Beget panel requires Beget-managed DNS/NS. With
  external DNS, use the technical domain or configure the CNAME externally.

## Origin

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Origin | `${BEGET_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}:${BEGET_ORIGIN_PORT}` |
| Protocol | HTTPS |
| Origin SNI/hostname | `${BEGET_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}` |
| Origin certificate mode | `${BEGET_ORIGIN_CERT_MODE}` |
| XHTTP path | `${BEGET_XHTTP_PATH}` |

Using an IP as the Beget origin is not recommended with the shared SNI router.
If it is unavoidable, Beget must send both TLS SNI and `Host` as
`${BEGET_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}`; an HTTP `Host` header alone is not sufficient for
the stream router.

## CDN behavior

- Use the same file-like XHTTP path `${BEGET_XHTTP_PATH}` on both sides, without
  a trailing slash. Session and sequence belong in query parameters
  `x_session` and `x_seq`, not in path segments.
- Use `xPaddingPlacement: header` with `X-Cache` on both sides. Do not use
  `queryInHeader` (a full URL in this header returned 403 in integration tests).

- Disable CDN and browser caching (or set the minimum CDN TTL of 1 second).
- Disable Always Online, following origin redirects and ignoring query params.
- Disable secure links, Referer/IP/User-Agent access policies for the first test.
- Disable HTTP/3, Gzip and large-file optimization/slicing.
- Allow `GET`, `HEAD` and `OPTIONS` (or leave the method whitelist disabled).
- Do not enable CORS rewriting or response headers on the CDN.
- If sessions break after 60-120 seconds, ask Beget support about increasing
  the origin timeout. Nginx is already configured for 3600 seconds.

## Checks

```bash
curl -4kso /dev/null -m 5 -w 'origin: %{http_code}\n' \
  --resolve "${BEGET_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}:443:${ORIGIN_IP}" \
  "https://${BEGET_ORIGIN_DOMAIN}${BEGET_XHTTP_PATH}"

curl -kso /dev/null -m 5 -w 'cdn: %{http_code}\n' \
  "https://${BEGET_HOST_DOMAIN}${BEGET_XHTTP_PATH}"
```

HTTP `400` from both requests is the expected response to a bare XHTTP GET.
This does not verify a complete VLESS session. Refresh the client subscription
and test actual traffic while watching the origin access/error logs. The CDN's
`x-reason-code: 7` alone does not identify the blocking rule.
